  "summary": "I've spent the better part of the last two decades immersed in the practical realities of enterprise software development. My philosophy is straightforward: I want to build reliable software that solves real problems. Spending my career since 2007 at the same organization means I don't just build systems and hand them off—I live through their entire lifecycle. I've learned firsthand the difference between a clever hack and a truly maintainable solution.\n\n​I thrive in the space between strategy and execution. My focus is on leading my team to cut through the noise, collaborating cross-functionally to make sound architectural trade-offs, and delivering secure, impactful software. Whether I'm deep in system architecture or mentoring a junior developer, my goal is to build things the right way so they stand the test of time.",
